WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.490
Speaker 1: On the Friday show, I am going
to be answering an audience question about

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:11.480
which Republicans are likely to get out of
the way if Donald Trump runs in 2024 versus

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:16.980
which Republicans are likely to run against
Trump in twenty twenty four.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.830
The list of the latter is probably relatively
short.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.270
I think Mitt Romney would be someone who is
on the list, even though I don't think Romney

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.890
plans to run.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.590
Romney is the type of guy who, if he wants
to run in twenty twenty four, he'll run against

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.140
Trump in the Republican primary.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:37.230
He won't step down or step back or stand by
because Donald Trump may choose to run.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:44.690
The new report from Axios is that Chris Christie's
friends believe he is gearing up for a 2024

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.739
run axios writing that former New Jersey Governor
Chris Christie is seriously considering running

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:51.420
for president in 2020.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.760
For three people familiar with his thinking,
tell Axios, while Christie isn't saying anything

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:02.149
publicly besides telling radio host Hugh Hewitt
that he's not ruling it out, people close

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:06.840
to Christie have a sense of the rationale
and outlines of a candidacy.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:12.749
The big picture is that absent a run by Trump,
the field would be wide open.

00:01:12.749 --> 00:01:15.959
Christie ran in 2016, didn't go well.

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:22.850
He told friends he'd be the only person in
2024 with executive experience who's run a

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.369
presidential race before.

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:30.469
I guess that's maybe true when you compare
him to like Ted Cruz.

00:01:30.469 --> 00:01:33.789
Ted Cruz has run, but he doesn't have executive
experience.

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:35.710
I guess that sort of makes sense.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:41.750
But Florida Governor Ron DeSantis has executive
experience for whatever reason.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.850
Governorships are called executive experience.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:48.380
I guess that's because there are more administrative
in a sense than, for example, being a member

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.289
of the House or a member of the U.S. Senate.

00:01:51.289 --> 00:01:56.840
DeSantis, as Axios writes, is experiencing
a surge of popularity from Republicans because

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.319
he opened Florida wide open very early.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:06.779
But DeSantis has not yet been scrutinized
by national media as a candidate and who knows

00:02:06.779 --> 00:02:09.360
what might surface from that.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.820
Axios writes that Christie's approach would
be to run on his reputation for being tough

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.090
and that that could appeal to the Trump base.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:21.360
But he's not going to come off as reckless
the way Donald Trump came off, you know, the

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:29.510
entire George Washington Bridge closing down
a lane as a political punishment.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.110
That seems pretty reckless to me.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.890
But I guess when you're comparing the recklessness
of Christie to the recklessness of Trump,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.170
he seems less.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:43.780
That's true, Axia Axios also writes that Chris
Christie may have crossover appeal to blue

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:49.990
collar voters as well as suburban center right
voters, that's possible and also that his

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.560
experience as a former federal prosecutor
could distinguish him in debates and prepare

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.950
him for a primary where there may be more
of a premium placed on sort of being buttoned

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.250
up rather than being unhinged like Donald
Trump.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.260
I think that this is tough for Chris Christie.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:17.570
You know, the things that he's known for really
in my mind are the Bridgegate fiasco and supporting

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:23.950
Donald Trump in completely humiliating fashion
in 2016.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:28.690
And neither of those are particularly inspiring
from my perspective.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:32.940
But listen, maybe the Republican primary voters
would would like it.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.620
Christie didn't do well in 2016.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.880
I don't know that he ever had more than like
two or three percent support.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.920
But listen, things are different.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:45.580
And I think what is abundantly clear is that
Christie is only a candidate if Trump does

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:53.310
not run and again, will dig into that in more
detail on Friday, who might actually run against

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.310
Trump?

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.600
Because Christie is only a candidate.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.410
If Trump is not, Ted Cruz isn't going to run
against Donald Trump.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.319
Lindsey Graham, forget about it.

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:03.340
Lindsey Graham, I don't think is running regardless.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.870
But Lindsey Graham is not going to run against
Donald Trump.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:12.640
Nikki Haley told us last week or was it Monday
that she if Donald Trump runs, she won't run

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:19.289
and she will support Donald Trump so that
that is the situation with Chris Christie.

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:23.050
I actually what's crazy is.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:30.360
If you said to me, whoever wins the Republican
primary will be the president.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.840
Chris Christie is maybe the guy I lean towards.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.710
I mean, if you say Chris Christie or Ted Cruz
will be the next president, I'm going with

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.930
Chris Christie.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:44.259
If you say Chris Christie or I don't even
know, you know, Rand Paul will be the next

00:04:44.259 --> 00:04:45.259
president.

00:04:45.259 --> 00:04:46.830
I'm going with Chris Christie.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:53.610
He has I'm not praising him, but he has more
centrist sensibilities.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:05:00.610
He actually seems competent in a narrow way
that Donald Trump is not.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.240
When you think about his experience as a prosecutor
and as a governor, he did horrible things

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.360
as a governor.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.460
Bridgegate is an immoral fiasco.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:14.639
But I probably lean towards someone like Chris
Christie more than just about anybody I can

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:16.629
think of that ran in.

00:05:16.629 --> 00:05:18.389
I mean, Kazik.

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:20.560
And again, I'm not saying these people are
my ideal candidates.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.430
It's just if I knew that the Republican nominee
would be the president, I'm leaning towards

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:29.080
someone like maybe Kasich or Chris Christie,
despite having many, many disagreements with

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.080
them.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.620
So let me know what you think about Chris
Christie's potential candidacy.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:37.879
We'll talk Friday about who might actually
fight Trump in the 2024 Republican primary

00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:38.939
if it were to come to that.

